{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"087d679e636e08063ee24ae523a193d831c5eb83530e7e4d4788bba6748c3e31","digest":{"component_or_area":"Jira Reconciler (fetcher.py)","key_entities":["fetcher.py","jql_active","jql_done_recent","statusCategory","status=Done","tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_fetch_multi_project.py","tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_fetch_paging_split.py","Gerrit change 1815","Gerrit change 1814"],"problem_keywords":["reconciler","jql","status category","active set","workflow","closed status","resolved status","scope"],"propositions":["jql_active query currently hardcodes status != 'Done' literal, which fails to exclude Closed/Resolved/Cancelled statuses in non-DIG/REB workflows, incorrectly pulling resolved issues into the active working set","jql_done_recent query hardcodes status = 'Done' literal, which misses Closed/Resolved/Cancelled statuses and fails to populate the recent-Done snapshot for non-standard workflows","Switching the Done predicate to statusCategory = Done / statusCategory != Done makes the reconciler workflow-agnostic and correctly scopes active/done sets across all Jira workflows","All existing single-project and multi-project fan-out behavior remains unchanged for DIG/REB workflows (To Do / In Progress / Done only statuses)"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787685792290113001,"uuid":"d383bb11-3156-48f7-b37b-310b559e4b2a"}